---
import BaseLayout from "../../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import MetaPill from "../../../components/ui/MetaPill.astro";
import registry from "../../../data/phase-82-household-capability-care-infrastructure-everyday-security-registry.json";

const capability = registry.household_capability_service_bundle_dossiers;
const care = registry.care_infrastructure_workforce_capacity_ledgers;
const burden = registry.household_affordability_time_debt_administrative_burden_registers;
const recovery = registry.neighborhood_access_displacement_crisis_recovery_ledgers;
---

<BaseLayout title="Household Capability, Care And Everyday Security | FTFN" description="Thirty-two inactive household-capability, care-infrastructure, burden, and neighborhood-recovery records.">
  <section class="page-section hero" data-household-capability-registry><div class="hero__copy"><div class="eyebrow">FTFN / Household Capability</div><h1 class="page-title">Service availability is not household capability, and temporary relief is not recovery.</h1><p class="lede">Phase 82 traces whether essential systems become usable household capability: adequate service bundles, care infrastructure and workforce, affordability across money and time, accessible neighborhoods, protection from displacement, crisis stabilization, and durable recovery.</p><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label="8 inactive capability dossiers" tone="possibility" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive care ledgers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive burden registers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive recovery ledgers" /><MetaPill label="0 household decisions" tone="review" /></div></div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Capability And Service Bundles</div><h2>Eight household-capability dossiers remain closed.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/household-capability-doctrine-001/">Read the capability doctrine</a></div><div class="grid">{capability.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.capability_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/household-capability/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Household boundaries, capability floors, service bundles, quality, time, care, resources, access, housing, transitions, distribution, options, funding, rights, review, and receipts remain empty.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Care Infrastructure And Workforce</div><h2>Eight care-capacity ledgers contain no finding.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/care-infrastructure-workforce-001/">Read the care-capacity guide</a></div><div class="grid">{care.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.care_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/household-capability/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.care_infrastructure_workforce_capacity_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Need, unpaid care, services, settings, capacity, workforce, providers, quality, access, affordability, coordination, respite, continuity, rights, and funding remain unassessed.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Affordability, Time, Debt And Administration</div><h2>Eight household-burden registers remain inactive.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/household-affordability-arrears-debt-001/">Read the household-affordability guide</a></div><div class="source-list">{burden.map((record) => <article class="source-row"><div><h3><a href={'/evidence/household-capability/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.household_affordability_time_debt_administrative_burden_register_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Resources, expenses, time, volatility, debt, arrears, administrative burden, take-up, shocks, stabilization, remedies, privacy, and distribution remain unmeasured.</p></div><MetaPill label={record.burden_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Neighborhood Access, Displacement And Recovery</div><h2>Eight neighborhood-recovery ledgers contain no intervention.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/crisis-stabilization-recovery-001/">Read the recovery guide</a></div><div class="grid">{recovery.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><h3><a href={'/evidence/household-capability/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.neighborhood_access_displacement_crisis_recovery_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Proximity, rural access, accessibility, social infrastructure, displacement, mobility, right to remain, crisis response, continuity, recovery, correction, learning, and audit remain inactive.</p><MetaPill label={record.recovery_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section briefing-band"><div class="briefing-band__copy"><div class="eyebrow">Public Contract</div><h2>Inspect the empty household-security state.</h2><p>The export publishes the complete control surface without assigning a household type, care need, service bundle, affordability finding, benefit access result, debt action, displacement finding, crisis response, recovery result, receipt, score, rank, or stage change.</p></div><article class="record-card"><a class="inline-link" href="/data/household-capability-care-everyday-security.json">Household capability JSON</a></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
